NAME
       poll, select - wait for a descriptor to become ready

SYNOPSIS
       #include <poll.h>

       int poll(struct pollfd *fds, nfds_t nfds, int timeout);

       #include <sys/select.h>

       int select(int nfds, fd_set *rfds, fd_set *wfds, fd_set *efds,
                  struct timeval *timeout);

DESCRIPTION
       Waits until one of the descriptors is ready, or until the
       timeout expires. For poll the timeout is in milliseconds; a
       negative value waits forever and zero returns at once.

       Each pollfd names a descriptor and the events wanted; the kernel
       fills in revents with what actually happened.

       POLLIN    data is available to read
       POLLOUT   writing will not block
       POLLERR   an error occurred
       POLLHUP   the peer hung up
       POLLNVAL  the descriptor is not open

RETURN VALUE
       The number of ready descriptors, 0 on timeout, or -1 with errno
       set.

ERRORS
       EINVAL   nfds is out of range
       EFAULT   fds points outside the address space
       EINTR    a signal arrived first

EXAMPLE
       Waiting for a key while animating, without busy-waiting:

              struct pollfd p = { 0, POLLIN, 0 };
              if (poll(&p, 1, 40) == 0)
                      next_frame();

SEE ALSO
       read(2), ioctl(2)
